  <static seed="258" source="csafranski/6.1HW_prob9.pg">
    <statement><p>Approximate the arc length of the curve <m>y=\frac{1}{4}x^4</m> over the interval <m>[1,2]</m> using the
trapezoidal rule and <m>8</m> intervals (i.e., <m>T_{8}</m>).</p>
<p><m>T_{8}=</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3.93785232683486</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Since <m>y=\frac14x^4</m>,
<me>1+(y')^2=1+(x^3)^2=1+x^6</me>
Therefore <m>\sqrt{1+y'^2}=\sqrt{1+x^6}</m> and the arc length over <m>[1,2]</m> is:
<me>\int_1^2\sqrt{1+x^6}dx</me></p>
<p>Let <m>f(x)=\sqrt{1+x^6}</m>. 
We take the estimate of the integral using the Trapezoidal Rule with 8 subdivisions. 
Since <m>n=8</m>,
<me>\Delta x=\frac{2-1}{8}</me>
<me>x_i=1+i\Delta x\:(i=0,\ldots,8)</me>
<me>y_i=f(1+i\Delta x)</me>
<me>T_{8}=\sum_{i=0}^{7}\frac12(y_i+y_{i+1})\Delta x</me></p>
<p>We have the table of approximations:
<div align="center"><table border="1"><tr><td>i</td><td>x<sub>i</sub></td><td>y<sub>i</sub></td><td>times</td><td>y<sub>i</sub>  2y<sub>i</sub></td></tr><tr><th>0</th><td>1</td><td>1.41421356</td><td>1</td><td> 1.41421356 </td></tr><tr><th>1</th><td>1.125</td><td>1.73990992</td><td>2</td><td> 3.47981984 </td></tr><tr><th>2</th><td>1.25</td><td>2.19424184</td><td>2</td><td> 4.38848369 </td></tr><tr><th>3</th><td>1.375</td><td>2.78531307</td><td>2</td><td> 5.57062614 </td></tr><tr><th>4</th><td>1.5</td><td>3.52003196</td><td>2</td><td> 7.04006392 </td></tr><tr><th>5</th><td>1.625</td><td>4.40599763</td><td>2</td><td> 8.81199526 </td></tr><tr><th>6</th><td>1.75</td><td>5.45187127</td><td>2</td><td> 10.9037425 </td></tr><tr><th>7</th><td>1.875</td><td>6.66721726</td><td>2</td><td> 13.3344345 </td></tr><tr><th>8</th><td>2</td><td>8.06225775</td><td>1</td><td> 8.06225775 </td></tr><tr><td/><td/><td>Total</td><td/><td>63.0056372</td></tr></table></div></p>
<p>From this, <m>T_{8}</m> is <m>\frac{1}{16}</m>
of the sum of the last column in the above table.</p>
<p>Thus, 
<me>\begin{array}{lcl} 
T_{8}\amp  = \amp  \frac{1}{16}(
1.41421356 + \cr \amp  \amp  + 3.47981984+4.38848369\cr \amp  \amp  + 5.57062614+7.04006392\cr \amp  \amp  + 8.81199526+10.9037425\cr \amp  \amp  + 13.3344345+8.06225775)
 \cr
\amp  = \amp  3.93785233 
\end{array}</me></p>
</solution>
